Update 1:
Looks like I found the cause of the problem. Objects annotated with @Configurable are initialized by AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect which implements BeanFactoryAware. This aspect uses BeanFactory to initialize beans. Looks like @PostConstruct method of the TestPostConstruct object is executed before BeanFactory is set to AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect. If logger set to debug the following message is printed to console: "BeanFactory has not been set on ...: Make sure this configurer runs in a Spring container. Unable to configure bean of type [...]. Proceeding without injection."
The question if there is any workaround is still open for me...

